Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 07/27/2023]
1.  Er = 1113 keV: standard resonance used to normalize strengths and cross sections of other resonances to; strength adopted from weighted average on Tab. III of 
    Lyons et al. 2018.
2.  Strengths of resonances listed in Endt & van der Leun 1978 were normalized using Er = 1113 keV.
3.  Partial widths were derived from wg and G when assumptions Gp << Gg or Gp >> Gg could be used.
4.  Er = 367 keV: we adopted the average strength of Endt and van der Leun 1978 [normalized to Lyons et al. 2018] and Masha et al. 2023. 
5.  Er = 1732 keV: energy and total width are averages from values discussed in Rolfs et al. 1975; Ex and G of Lyons et al. are not used because they were obtained 
    from an R matrix analysis and RatesMC uses Breit-Wigner amplitudes.   
6.  Er = 2037 keV: no uncertainty on wg is given in Endt & van der Leun 1978; assumed here 30%.
7.  Er = -7 keV: Gg from DSAM lifetime measured in Anttila et al. 1977; reduced width from C2S reported in Mukhamedzanow et al. 2006 (0.59), Terakawa et al. 1993
    (1.0), and shell-model value (0.65).
8.  Direct capture: used C2S from Mukhamedzanov et al. 2006 (3He,d), Terakawa et al. 1993 (d,n), Datta et al. 1979 (d,p), and shell model; main DC contribution is
    from DC -> 2424 keV [subthreshold state]; assumed 20% uncertainty in total S factor.


